        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "5fbcc6ad-682f-5a0c-805d-f25c470312d2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Sila Region, Chad, Libya, Sudan, Central African Republic, Cameroon, Nigeria, Niger, Markounda, Tripoli\n- Organizations: Gurgi Mosque\n- Topics: borders, administrative creation\n\nFacts:\n- Sila Region in Chad was created in 2008 from the departments of Sila and Djourf Al Ahmar, which had previously been part of Ouaddaï Region.\n- Chad is bordered by Libya to the north, Sudan to the east, the Central African Republic to the south, Cameroon and Nigeria to the southwest, and Niger to the west.\n- Markounda is a sub-prefecture that borders Chad.\n- Gurgi Mosque is a mosque in Tripoli, Libya.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
