        "text": "Page: Sila Region. Sentence: Sila or Dar Sila is a region of Chad which was created in 2008 from the departments of Sila and Djourf Al Ahmar previously part of Ouaddaï Region.\nPage: Chad. Sentence: It is bordered by Libya to the north, Sudan to the east, the Central African Republic to the south, Cameroon and Nigeria to the southwest and Niger to the west.\nPage: Markounda. Sentence: The sub-prefecture borders with Chad.\nPage: Gurgi Mosque. Sentence: Gurgi Mosque is a mosque in Tripoli, Libya.",
